# FP&A / feature delivery checklist (NVCCZ)

When the user asks you to **implement** a new FP&A (or comparable backend) feature from FE/API requirements, finish this pipeline in the **same turn**:

1. **Implement** code + idempotent migration script + `package.json` `db:migrate:…` entry.
2. **Dedicated API docs** — separate markdown under `docs/` (e.g. `docs/fpa-*-api.md`). Include endpoints, request/response examples, enums, errors, acceptance checklist.
3. **Migrate all three MySQL DBs**: `nts`, `client1_db`, `demo_env` (override `DATABASE_URL`; same pattern as existing `scripts/run-*-all-dbs-vps.py` or local remote MySQL URLs). **After** the migrate loop, **unset** shell `DATABASE_URL` so UAT/dev use `.env` → **`nts` only**.
4. **UAT / seed with real client-demo data** — **always on DEV `nts`** (see `nvccz-uat-dev-db-only.mdc`). Never UAT against `client1_db` / `demo_env`. Scripts must create or reuse story-ready fixtures (named departments, owners, cycles). Prefer Arcus / existing `db:seed:fpa-demo` entities. Log IDs and names clearly in UAT output.
5. **Do NOT commit, push, or VPS-deploy** unless the user explicitly asks in that turn.

## Explicit overrides

| User says | Do |
|-----------|-----|
| “push and deploy” / “commit and push” | Then commit / push / deploy as asked |
| “no migrate” | Skip 3-DB migrate |

Do not offer “say if you want deploy” as the default stop — migrations + docs + client-demo UAT **are** required; push/deploy are **opt-in**.
